{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://github.com/chris-dare-dev/math-formal-contract-lean/schema/resolution-1.0.schema.json",
  "title": "resolution/1.0 - the one artifact arXMCP produces",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "registry_sha256",
    "notebook",
    "corpus_version",
    "corpus_manifest_content_hash",
    "resolver_version",
    "chunker_version",
    "generated_at",
    "results",
    "counts"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "const": "resolution/1.0"
    },
    "registry_sha256": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
      "$comment": "THE ENTIRE CROSS-REPO FRESHNESS MECHANISM. One comparison, no clocks, no mtimes, no network. Editing the registry without re-running the resolver turns CI red, and there is no way to forget."
    },
    "notebook": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
    },
    "corpus_version": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 0
    },
    "corpus_manifest_content_hash": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"
    },
    "resolver_version": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "chunker_version": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "generated_at": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "results": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/result"
      }
    },
    "counts": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "current",
        "drifted",
        "unresolvable",
        "paper_absent",
        "not_run"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "current": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "drifted": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "unresolvable": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "paper_absent": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        },
        "not_run": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 0
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "$defs": {
    "result": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "key",
        "resolution",
        "matched_by",
        "chunk_id",
        "matched_body_sha256",
        "printed_number",
        "similarity",
        "reason",
        "resolved_source_version"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "key": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^stmt:[0-9a-f]{12}:[a-z][a-z0-9._-]{0,63}$"
        },
        "resolution": {
          "enum": [
            "current",
            "drifted",
            "unresolvable",
            "paper_absent",
            "not_run"
          ]
        },
        "matched_by": {
          "enum": [
            "quote_sha256",
            "quote_containment",
            "printed_number",
            "fuzzy",
            "none"
          ],
          "$comment": "Ordered strongest to weakest. `quote_sha256` is byte-equality after normalization. `quote_containment` -- the chunk body CONTAINS the normalized quote -- is what actually survives a re-chunk that merges or splits the statement's chunk, and it reads `current`: containment is an identity claim, not a similarity score, which is why it sits above `fuzzy` and not beside it. `fuzzy` may never read `current`; similarity is not identity."
        },
        "chunk_id": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "resolved_source_version": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "$comment": "The source version this result was resolved against -- the arXiv vN, or null. Null is currently the ONLY honest value: the corpus records arxiv_version as '' for every row in every notebook (8/8 sampled in each), so nothing can fill this until the ingest backfill lands. It is present and nullable rather than absent so that a resolution which CAN say which version it read has somewhere to say it, and one that cannot is visibly silent rather than silently unversioned."
        },
        "matched_body_sha256": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"
        },
        "printed_number": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "similarity": {
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ],
          "minimum": 0,
          "maximum": 1
        },
        "reason": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "$comment": "`current` REQUIRES a recomputed body digest. A resolver that says current without showing its work is rejected.",
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "resolution": {
                "const": "current"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "resolution"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "required": [
              "matched_body_sha256",
              "chunk_id"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "matched_body_sha256": {
                "type": "string",
                "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"
              },
              "chunk_id": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "$comment": "A FUZZY match can NEVER be current. Nearest-neighbour similarity is not identity - this is the single line that stops a dense-ANN retrieval system silently re-pointing a citation at a different theorem.",
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "matched_by": {
                "const": "fuzzy"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "matched_by"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "resolution": {
                "enum": [
                  "drifted",
                  "unresolvable"
                ]
              },
              "similarity": {
                "type": "number"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "$comment": "printed_number is a HINT. It is populated only on the ar5iv/LaTeXML path (36 of 66 chunks even on the flagship paper), and authors renumber between versions.",
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "matched_by": {
                "const": "printed_number"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "matched_by"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "resolution": {
                "enum": [
                  "drifted"
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "$comment": "`quote_containment` may read `current`, and that is the whole point of the rung: containment is an IDENTITY claim -- the statement is in the chunk or it is not -- where `fuzzy` is an estimate. It still owes the same evidence as any other current result (the first conditional above), and it must carry NO similarity score: a number there would invite exactly the reading that this is a near-miss.",
          "if": {
            "properties": {
              "matched_by": {
                "const": "quote_containment"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "matched_by"
            ]
          },
          "then": {
            "properties": {
              "resolution": {
                "enum": [
                  "current",
                  "drifted",
                  "unresolvable"
                ]
              },
              "similarity": {
                "type": "null"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
